From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: EDEN_NX2_NATIVE_TABLES=compute+mesh keeps pointers
 read through memory for task and mesh programs

Core patch on mig020-core (T42), a new value of an existing switch. Unset and every value used so far
behave as before.

T42 runs with EDEN_NX2_NATIVE_TABLES=compute, and that mode takes the =0 path for task and mesh
programs: a pointer read through memory a constant buffer pointer points to is not bound, and the
access stays global, which reads 0 outside the bound storage buffers. Duck912's message on Lichii
bf3f395c96 says Ocarina's grass task and mesh programs load their pool base that way, and that reads
of 0 made the task shader cull every blade. Our patch 0201 says the same in its header: only worth
setting with tables on and mesh draws running. So mesh draws with =compute are expected to run and
still show no grass. This value is the one to use for a plant test.

It leaves vertex and fragment programs on the =0 path, the part of a tables run that costs memory in
every draw's bindings. A pointer read through memory comes back as an indirect binding, so
EDEN_NX2_TABLE_POOL_MIB applies to it in BindGraphicsStorageBuffer. Table entries stay compute only;
Lichii's pass has the same rule for graphics stages, so task and mesh programs reach what they reach
there.

Not built, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp
@@ -1107,8 +1107,11 @@
 /// pointer, the part of a tables run that costs memory in every draw's bindings. A run with
 /// tables on dies on memory (run56, translating mesh programs): this says whether the compute
 /// side alone changes the picture.
+/// EDEN_NX2_NATIVE_TABLES=compute+mesh: as compute, and task and mesh programs keep those pointers
+/// too, with mesh draws running again. Vertex and fragment programs still take the =0 path, and
+/// table entries stay compute only (below).
 bool NativeTablesEnabled(Stage stage) {
-    enum class Mode { Off, Compute, On };
+    enum class Mode { Off, Compute, ComputeMesh, On };
     static const Mode mode = [] {
         const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_NATIVE_TABLES");
         if (value == nullptr) {
@@ -1120,9 +1123,13 @@
         if (std::string_view{value} == "compute") {
             return Mode::Compute;
         }
+        if (std::string_view{value} == "compute+mesh") {
+            return Mode::ComputeMesh;
+        }
         return Mode::On;
     }();
-    return mode == Mode::On || (mode == Mode::Compute && stage == Stage::Compute);
+    return mode == Mode::On || (mode != Mode::Off && stage == Stage::Compute) ||
+           (mode == Mode::ComputeMesh && (stage == Stage::Task || stage == Stage::Mesh));
 }
 
 /// Native programs: every constant buffer pointer the low address can come from, following only
